# Workshop Code of Conduct
  
## Our Commitment
This workshop welcomes participants across disciplines, career stages, and institutions. We build every session on mutual respect, and we ask each participant to help create a space where everyone can contribute fully.

## Participation Expectations
- Listen actively and build on others' ideas rather than dismissing them.
- Value contributions equally, regardless of discipline, career stage, or institution.
- Use correct names and pronouns, and take care to pronounce names accurately.
- Direct disagreement at ideas, not people, and keep critique constructive.
- Explain field-specific terms so colleagues from other disciplines can follow.

## Sharing the Floor
Because this workshop depends on hearing many voices, we ask everyone to:
- Keep contributions concise (roughly under a minute) so more people can speak.
- Practice “step up, step back”: speak up if you haven't contributed yet, and make room if you've already spoken several times.
- Treat a facilitator's redirect (“Let's hear from someone new”) as normal, healthy facilitation — not a personal correction.
- Use sticky notes, shared docs, or chat during breakouts so quieter voices can contribute in more than one way.
- Expect structured formats (round-robin turns, timed responses, small breakouts and raised hands)
- Facilitator Role
- Facilitators actively manage time and airtime. They may redirect, pause, or gently interrupt any speaker, regardless of seniority, to protect space for other participants, and they will invite quieter participants directly (“[Name], what's your take?”). We ask everyone to receive these interventions as good facilitation, not as disrespect.

## Respectful Communication
Participants avoid interrupting, talking over others, and dismissive language or body language. We do not tolerate discriminatory or harassing conduct related to race, gender, nationality, career stage, or institutional affiliation.

## Raising a Concern
Any participant can raise a concern privately with a facilitator or organizer at any time. Organizers will handle every concern promptly and with discretion.

